# AMENDMENT No. 2 TO THE MASTER SERVICES AGREEMENT

Reference KCC/MSA/2023/017-A2 — Signed version — Privileged until signature, thereafter CONFIDENTIAL

This Amendment No. 2 (the "Amendment") is made on 29 August 2024 between Korvane Cold Chain Sp. z o.o. of ul. Łużycka 14, 81-537 Gdynia ("Korvane") and Oakhaven Dairy Ltd of Fenwick Lane Farm, Nantwich, Cheshire CW5 8QT ("the Customer").

## Background

(A) The parties are bound by a Master Services Agreement dated 3 April 2023, reference KCC/MSA/2023/017, as already amended by Amendment No. 1 of 20 November 2023, which added the Gdynia–Kłaipėda feeder lane to Schedule 1 and changed nothing else (the "MSA").

(B) On 14 June 2024 a Temperature Excursion of 9 hours affected a Consignment of Chilled Dairy Products carried for the Customer (the "Incident"). By letter dated 28 June 2024 the Customer's solicitors, Marlowe Pinfold LLP of Manchester, claimed EUR 311,800 from Korvane in respect of the Incident.

(C) Korvane does not admit liability for the sum claimed or any part of it. The parties nevertheless wish to settle the Incident and to adjust the MSA for the future, and have agreed as follows. Words defined in the MSA keep their meaning here.

## 1. Effect and commencement

1.1 Save for clause 7 of this Amendment, which takes effect on signature, this Amendment takes effect on 1 October 2024 (the "Amendment Effective Date"). The changes below apply to every Temperature Excursion that begins on or after the Amendment Effective Date; the Incident and any earlier excursion remain governed by the MSA as it stood before this Amendment, subject to the settlement in clause 7.

## 2. Alert time

2.1 In clause 4.2 of the MSA the words "within 20 minutes" are deleted and replaced with "within 10 minutes".

## 3. Service credits

3.1 Clause 4.3 and Table A of Schedule 2 of the MSA are deleted and replaced as follows.

3.2 New clause 4.3: Where a Temperature Excursion occurs, Korvane shall grant the Customer a service credit calculated by applying to the Affected Fee the percentage set out in the new Table A of Schedule 2 against the relevant Excursion Hours. Excursions of 30 minutes or less do not qualify and generate no credit.

3.3 New Table A — Temperature Excursion service credits (percentage of the Affected Fee), applicable from the Amendment Effective Date:

| Excursion Hours | Service credit |
|---|---|
| more than 0.5 and up to 2.0 hours | 8% |
| more than 2.0 and up to 4.0 hours | 15% |
| more than 4.0 and up to 8.0 hours | 30% |
| more than 8.0 and up to 12.0 hours | 50% |
| more than 12.0 and up to 24.0 hours | 75% |
| more than 24.0 hours | 100% |

3.4 In clause 4.5 of the MSA "25%" is replaced by "40%" and "within 30 days" is replaced by "within 45 days". The rest of clause 4.5 is unchanged.

3.5 The reference in clause 4.4 of the MSA to "the percentage stated in Table A" is to be read as a reference to the new Table A.

## 4. Enhanced monitoring (new clause 4.7)

4.1 A new clause 4.7 is inserted in the MSA: "From the Amendment Effective Date Korvane shall fit a second KC-Tag 4 logger, placed at the door end of the container, to every container carrying the Customer's Chilled Dairy Products, at no additional charge. Where the two loggers disagree, the logger showing the higher Excursion Hours governs. Korvane and the Customer shall meet quarterly to review excursions and alert performance, the first meeting to be held in the week commencing 13 January 2025."

## 5. Liability and insurance

5.1 In clause 7.2 of the MSA "EUR 85,000" is replaced by "EUR 120,000". The recall-cost limit of EUR 200,000 per event in the same clause is not altered, and nor is clause 7.1.

5.2 In clause 9.1(a) of the MSA "EUR 4,000,000" is replaced by "EUR 6,000,000". Korvane shall procure from Seaboard Insurance Brokers a certificate evidencing the increased cover and deliver it to the Customer within 15 Business Days after the Amendment Effective Date.

## 6. Termination

6.1 Clause 14.2 of the MSA is deleted and replaced as follows: "After the first anniversary of the Effective Date Korvane may terminate this Agreement for convenience by giving the Customer not less than 180 days' written notice, and the Customer may terminate it for convenience by giving Korvane not less than 120 days' written notice. Notice under this clause or clause 14.1 must be sent by courier or registered post; e-mail alone is not sufficient."

6.2 A new clause 14.5 is inserted: "If (a) any Temperature Excursion has Excursion Hours exceeding 12, or (b) two Temperature Excursions each exceeding 4 hours occur within any rolling period of 90 days, the Customer may terminate this Agreement on 30 days' written notice, provided that the notice is given within 60 days after the event under (a) or after the second excursion under (b). Termination under this clause 14.5 gives rise to no liability for early termination."

## 7. Settlement of the Incident

7.1 In full and final settlement of every claim, whether or not yet notified, arising from the Incident (including cargo loss, rejection, recall, retailer chargebacks and the sums claimed in the letter of 28 June 2024), and without any admission of liability, Korvane shall pay the Customer EUR 96,400.00 on or before 13 September 2024 to the account the Customer's Finance Director has notified in writing. Korvane shall in addition contribute EUR 4,200.00 towards the Customer's legal costs, payable on the same date. Each party otherwise bears its own costs.

7.2 On receipt of both sums the Customer releases Korvane from all claims arising from the Incident. The release does not extend to claims for death or personal injury or to any matter unconnected with the Incident.

7.3 The terms of this clause 7 are confidential. Either party may disclose them to its insurers, brokers, auditors and professional advisers, and Korvane shall notify its cargo insurer of the settlement without delay. Neither party shall make any public statement about the Incident.

## 8. General

8.1 Save as amended here the MSA remains in full force and effect. If this Amendment and the MSA conflict, this Amendment prevails. Clause 17 of the MSA (Polish law, escalation, exclusive jurisdiction of the Regional Court in Gdańsk) applies to this Amendment. It may be signed in counterparts.

Signed at Gdynia on 29 August 2024 for Korvane Cold Chain Sp. z o.o. by Marta Kowarzik (Chief Executive Officer) and Priya Venkataraman-Holt (Chief Financial Officer); for Oakhaven Dairy Ltd by Gwendolen Pryce-Aldous (Managing Director).

*Drafting history: v3 of 21 August 2024 had the settlement at EUR 88,000 and a 150-day Customer notice; superseded by the figures above after the call of 27 August. SB.*
